{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/54785-just-purchased-wtf-how-do-i-put-a-pack-together-for-new-players-to-wod","id":54785,"title":"Just purchased WtF - how do I put a pack together for new players to WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-21T11:33:47-08:00","id":54785,"title":"Just purchased WtF - how do I put a pack together for new players to WoD","content":"So I have made my first NWoD purchase(other than the core book). I'm reading through it, and it seems to make a lot of assumptions about the players knowing about the world.. or it may be me.<br /> I'm trying to get my head around how to bring all the players together to form a pack. And it's just not clicking...yet. It maybe from the years upon years of d20 indoctrination that has skewed my GM brain... so help, please?<br /> <br /> What are some ways you have done or are doing to bring your game together and get the ball rolling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2066-jhilahd","name":"jhilahd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:46:58-08:00","id":54796,"title":"","content":"The Quickstart contains an adventure called <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/2360?affiliate_id=22713&amp;src=OPPForums\" target=\"_blank\">The Hunt Begins</a>, which might be a place to start with new PCs.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:31:34-08:00","id":54825,"title":"","content":"There's another book out there for World of Darkness called <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/2393/World-of-Darkness-Mysterious-Places?term=mysterious+&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mysterious Places</a>, it's full of all kinds of plot hooks to drag characters into the same situation from different places and angles. Get that, if you can, and try a few, or dream up a few ideas of your own about how to bring all the characters together. After that, you can initiate them into the Forsaken world as a group with yourself as some NPC mentors and such, and that will help get them on their feet.<br /> <br /> Another option is to give them a rundown of &quot;Forsaken 101&quot; after you know the material well yourself. It's a good time to have everyone make their characters, too. Let them know what you know and that you don't know it all yet, but here's what you've got. Then you all learn it together.<br /> <br /> Or, as Matt has above, the quick-start method. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If the pre-made adventures suit you and your group, look at the SAS stuff on DriveThruRPG for Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:57:31-08:00","id":54842,"title":"","content":"What I did was to allow them to be related and thrown together to take over some territory that a lager and more experienced pack couldn't keep with th Pure knocking on their door. Worked well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T13:47:02-08:00","id":54875,"title":"","content":"Freak incidents work out well. I was gonna have my pack come together at an intersection suddenly wrought with traffic accidents (major ones), particularly the one they were in. With no discernable reason to see for the accident the wolves could &quot;sniff&quot; each other out, then find a way into the hisil, seeing a massive magath (Semi with a car trailer mixed with western diamond back rattle snakes), and a temp pack forms from that. Then the need to cover a territory... yada yada. I also had ideas for ridden and levels of ridden if you were interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T13:50:33-08:00","id":54878,"title":"","content":"Oh! There is also the free demo on drive through rpg. Manitou springs i think it is. The chroniclers guide also has some fun storyline concepts in there as well. Particularly the ziggeraut if you want uratha with the control over the garou form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:03:40-08:00","id":54886,"title":"","content":"Yeah most of the stuff in the Core is considered to be general knowledge to Werewolves (more or less). The idea being that during their initiation period where they're introduced to a tribe and learn about their mythology, they're told some basic information about what they are. Granted this can seem to be a problem if you're playing a mortal-to-werewolf game, but then you can take care of it by having there be a learning period so after they get hooked up with a mentor pack or whatever they're told the basics.<br /> <br /> As for how the pack can get together, they could be the only ones native to a certain area (which then becomes their territory), they could be given an area by whichever pack or packs watches over a territory, they could have some sort of spiritual connection to it that links them together (perhaps when they went through their first change they earned the friendship of a totem spirit who lives in a specific spot), maybe they were all at a werewolf moot and, having no territory, were sent to some place that needs tending. Or maybe they all met in a bar and, realizing they were on the same side, decided to team up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:05:39-08:00","id":54940,"title":"","content":"What I did was I just said that their various mentors who found them after the first change put them together as a pack. Not especially epic, but it got the job done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1187-prons","name":"Prons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:45:07-08:00","id":54969,"title":"","content":"There's another WoD book called Dogs of War that's all about military life and such. You could have them part of some secret military project that uses them as a SpecOps clean up crew. As mentioned above Mysterious Places is another great book to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:07:52-08:00","id":55159,"title":"","content":"Wow. Thanks for the replies. I guess, I was struggling more with the mortal-to-werewolf/tribe-to-pack focus. Seeing how to incorporate those aspects instead of just saying &quot;Hey you're all recently changed members of your tribes, you've undergone your rite of passage and have been called to X to observe a passing of something-something&quot; Or something like that.<br /> <br /> Was and still am, more worried about getting info across to my players so they feel a part of this... I might just be over thinking this also...<br /> Thanks again, great stuff and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2066-jhilahd","name":"jhilahd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:01:24-08:00","id":55244,"title":"","content":"So it's plot hooks you're looking for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\"> 1001 Werewolf Story Hooks - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Reposting my old 1001 Werewolf Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful. Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I created this thread on three separate fora. 1) The PC pack has reason to believe that the alpha of a neighboring Forsaken pack has been corrupted </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:00:34-08:00","id":55531,"title":"","content":"You could always have them start as ghost wolves, and have recruiters from various tribes popping up as npcs, OR you could just have em all bitten by the fire touched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:27:41-08:00","id":55543,"title":"","content":"My longest W:tF chronicle began with the pack members all being the junior members of a larger pack of veteran Uratha. The first session started with them sitting in a pub, watching the tv news report with horror as it panned across the flaming wreckage that had been the pack's main holding. A large Pure pack had attacked, and the elders had sent the fresh newbies out of harms way to keep them safe, then got wiped out as they defended their turf (well, all but one, but he went into hiding due to, among other things, being a Bale Hound).<br /> <br /> The Pure then retreated, having finished their mission (who they were and why they had performed the attack was one of the long-running elements in the chronicle), leaving the fledgeling werewolves to then try to pick up the pieces that their dead mentors had left behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:58:56-08:00","id":55554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/54785-just-purchased-wtf-how-do-i-put-a-pack-together-for-new-players-to-wod?p=55543#post55543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My longest W:tF chronicle began with the pack members all being the junior members of a larger pack of veteran Uratha. The first session started with them sitting in a pub, watching the tv news report with horror as it panned across the flaming wreckage that had been the pack's main holding. A large Pure pack had attacked, and the elders had sent the fresh newbies out of harms way to keep them safe, then got wiped out as they defended their turf (well, all but one, but he went into hiding due to, among other things, being a Bale Hound).<br /> <br /> The Pure then retreated, having finished their mission (who they were and why they had performed the attack was one of the long-running elements in the chronicle), leaving the fledgeling werewolves to then try to pick up the pieces that their dead mentors had left behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice one. I'll steal that one if I get a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:28:35-08:00","id":56188,"title":"","content":"On the topic of new players, I've this woman who has no concept of &quot;Uratha shouldnt breed&quot;, and wants her character to shack up with her boyfriends character. She is rather insistent of it, and pouts quite furiously (while tossing her character sheet) when I tell her they'll have no children. I think instead of shooting it down outright, I should instead turn it into an opportunity for corruption. Bale hound of lust anyone? Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T10:48:42-08:00","id":56226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/54785-just-purchased-wtf-how-do-i-put-a-pack-together-for-new-players-to-wod?p=56188#post56188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of new players, I've this woman who has no concept of &quot;Uratha shouldnt breed&quot;, and wants her character to shack up with her boyfriends character. She is rather insistent of it, and pouts quite furiously (while tossing her character sheet) when I tell her they'll have no children. I think instead of shooting it down outright, I should instead turn it into an opportunity for corruption. Bale hound of lust anyone? Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that. I'm not quite familiar with the Bale Hounds though, so I'll throw out some other ideas. Let them go through with it and get caught and all the neighboring packs denounce them, or let her get pregnant and have a Unihar. If that doesn't drive the point home, nothing will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T12:53:54-08:00","id":56298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/54785-just-purchased-wtf-how-do-i-put-a-pack-together-for-new-players-to-wod?p=56188#post56188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of new players, I've this woman who has no concept of &quot;Uratha shouldnt breed&quot;, and wants her character to shack up with her boyfriends character. She is rather insistent of it, and pouts quite furiously (while tossing her character sheet) when I tell her they'll have no children. I think instead of shooting it down outright, I should instead turn it into an opportunity for corruption. Bale hound of lust anyone? Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha SHOULD breed (Cleave to the Human and all that)... Not sure where you got the idea that they should not. They should breed with <i><b>HUMANS</b></i>, though, and not other Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:48:50-08:00","id":56558,"title":"","content":"Well thats what i meant. Breed with each other. They'd both be werewolves, so incestuous relationships and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:10:23-08:00","id":56725,"title":"","content":"Ahhhhh.... Then no, no werewolf boom-boom for her... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Unless, of course, you want to explore the possibilities of a Black Birth. That is a cool story.<br /> One of our first campaigns centered around trying to make right the consequences of a Black Birth that had occurred. Lost a few characters in that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 01-24-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:27:54-08:00","id":56734,"title":"","content":"Our first game had more than a little werewolf on werewolf action. To make matters worse, one of the significant others was a Pure (though we didn't know that, at first). We saw a unihar being birthed at a moot, but it didn't really stop much. The character fell, went Bale Hound and died.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, it happens. If a character wants to do it you shouldn't stop them (though you should let them know how it would seem to others in the context of the situation, like incest coupled with the birthing of a werewolf-hating monstrosity), the other characters are fully within their rights to disapprove and show their disapproval. NPCs, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru